sqrt{30}/2$, and C, $\\sqrt{7.5}$, are both exactly equal to $\\sqrt{15}/\\sqrt2$. There is no unique correct choice. The question is repeated at D21-P047-Q018.","bank_review_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"},"reasons":["Retain held source and link the independently checked supported-response version."]},{"id":"af2c2124-569a-56d4-9b36-a22cf8f089cd","row_hash":"e4a6446da74cee6b958c3a5013da3917","key_hash":"f6c933935aee7d79b35eca1c8080d4e6","fields":{},"assets_remove":[],"assets_merge":{"replacement_question_id":"cefc1468-7880-55a1-9eb2-d84b876b5c60","replacement_review_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","replacement_review_note":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Printed stem says the total diameters of 15 plates of diameter 7 or 12 inches is 14 inches; this is impossible. Options use 140, which would require correcting the source.","bank_review_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"},"reasons":["Retain held source and link the independently checked supported-response version."]},{"id":"ec6acdfa-1dab-561f-ab3a-fd7a542c2ea6","row_hash":"db41114008875cb376ccbb4b64f07d6f","key_hash":"84773360b6cccfed12e0a35539d4737c","fields":{},"assets_remove":[],"assets_merge":{"replacement_question_id":"ad96f85f-6241-54dd-8d5b-0d1d297676a9","replacement_review_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","replacement_review_note":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The parameter a is unrestricted, so when a=0 the system has infinitely many solutions; two choices also contain an unbound y/a. A unique complete solution cannot be certified without adding assumptions.","bank_review_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"},"reasons":["Retain held source and link the independently checked supported-response version."]}],"additions":[{"id":"91a7a5bf-b1b8-51ac-9a5b-8dedb72ed64f","track_id":"act2","topic":"Logarithms and exponentials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For real x ≠ 0, y > 0, and z > 0, which expression equals $\\ln\\left(\\frac{x^2\\sqrt y}{z}\\right)$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$2\\ln|x|+\\frac12\\ln y-\\ln z$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2\\ln|x|+2\\ln y-\\ln z$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\ln|x|+\\frac12\\ln y-\\ln z$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2\\ln|x|+\\frac12\\ln y+\\ln z$"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"The quotient rule subtracts ln z. The power rules give ln(x²) = 2 ln|x| and ln(√y) = ½ ln y. The absolute value is necessary because x may be negative.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["074ada07-ac7e-53b6-adf6-0f9d4b5baf9d"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P016-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Logarithms and exponentials","lesson_subtopic":"Logarithms and exponentials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"7f4aefc3-6447-5a2c-86da-69e65b787219","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the real domain of $h(x)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5-x}}{x+2}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"x < 5"},{"key":"B","text":"x ≥ 5 and x ≠ −2"},{"key":"C","text":"All real x except −2"},{"key":"D","text":"x ≤ 5 and x ≠ −2"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"The square root requires 5 − x ≥ 0, or x ≤ 5. The denominator must be nonzero, so x ≠ −2. The endpoint x = 5 is allowed.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["09ecb437-4fe7-557d-80f8-dcd74efcc638"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P008-Q002"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Functions and transformations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"4ba3a6bf-3235-599b-8e77-dba0f96dc9d3","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What are the vertical and horizontal asymptotes of $y=\\frac{2x+1}{x-3}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"x = 3 and y = 1/2"},{"key":"B","text":"x = −1/2 and y = 3"},{"key":"C","text":"x = 3 and y = 2"},{"key":"D","text":"x = −3 and y = 2"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"At x = 3 the denominator is zero and numerator is 7, so x = 3 is a vertical asymptote. Equal polynomial degrees give horizontal asymptote y = 2/1 = 2.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["0eea2617-8e7a-50e6-98da-152f0ba6399b"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P013-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Rational expressions","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"405063fb-1cda-510e-a298-e2c8adfe6194","track_id":"act2","topic":"Inequalities and absolute value","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the complete real solution set of $2|x-4|=9$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\{-5,13\\}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\{-\\frac12,\\frac{17}2\\}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\{\\frac12,\\frac{17}2\\}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\{-\\frac12,\\frac92\\}$"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Divide by 2: |x − 4| = 9/2. Thus x = 4 ± 9/2, giving −1/2 and 17/2.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["1598aea2-88e9-57a6-91d4-c0fb8006ccc7","6cb27c03-9ab5-5513-ab59-b2554829b6f7"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D17-P038-Q038","ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P037-Q096"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Source has no answer choices. Equation2|x−4|=9 has solutions−1/2 and17/2; do not create options.","curriculum_lesson":"Inequalities and absolute value","lesson_subtopic":"Inequalities and absolute value","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"1aba05bd-f31c-58b7-9105-4421e370c33a","track_id":"act2","topic":"Complex numbers","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For $i^2=-1$, what is $i^{37}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"i"},{"key":"B","text":"−i"},{"key":"C","text":"1"},{"key":"D","text":"−1"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Powers of i repeat every four powers. Since 37 = 4(9) + 1, i³⁷ = (i⁴)⁹i = i.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["16b328b4-5d7c-5bc5-bef8-72bc866070cd"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P012-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Complex numbers","lesson_subtopic":"Complex numbers","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"8843f032-e921-5a52-ba56-30a7a202af73","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"The function y = 2x − 4 has domain {−4, 0, 6}. What is its range?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"{−8, 0, 12}"},{"key":"B","text":"{−12, 0, 8}"},{"key":"C","text":"{−4, 0, 6}"},{"key":"D","text":"{−12, −4, 8}"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Evaluate each input: 2(−4) − 4 = −12; 2(0) − 4 = −4; 2(6) − 4 = 8.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["172ad291-1971-5b92-80b0-8e96aaa0840b"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P033-Q086"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The response is a three-element range set and choices are absent; scalar numeric grading is unsuitable.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Functions and transformations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"94c1ad64-0fca-5d8a-9d0b-c389810da2df","track_id":"act2","topic":"Circles","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which equation represents a circle with center (−2,5) and radius 4?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(x + 2)² + (y − 5)² = 4"},{"key":"B","text":"(x − 2)² + (y − 5)² = 4"},{"key":"C","text":"(x + 2)² + (y − 5)² = 16"},{"key":"D","text":"(x − 2)² + (y + 5)² = 16"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"A circle with center (h,k) and radius r satisfies (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r². Substituting h = −2, k = 5, and r = 4 gives choice A.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["17976d6c-2ce8-5351-ab19-3ebc0e121401"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P024-Q002"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Circles","lesson_subtopic":"Circles","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"71a87f1b-2153-5161-9618-381aa950b157","track_id":"act2","topic":"Matrices","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is $\\begin{pmatrix}2&1\\\\-3&4\\end{pmatrix}+\\begin{pmatrix}5&-2\\\\1&6\\end{pmatrix}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}-3&3\\\\-4&-2\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}7&-1\\\\-2&10\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}7&3\\\\-4&10\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}10&-2\\\\-3&24\\end{pmatrix}$"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Add corresponding entries: 2 + 5 = 7, 1 − 2 = −1, −3 + 1 = −2, and 4 + 6 = 10.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["26abc145-8b08-53fb-adc9-a7f97337dd01"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P026-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Matrices","lesson_subtopic":"Matrices","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"1295d970-be8f-5b87-87a4-7807f1af0f51","track_id":"act2","topic":"Systems of equations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which ordered pair (x,y) solves 2x + y = 11 and x − y = 1?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(4,3)"},{"key":"B","text":"(3,4)"},{"key":"C","text":"(5,1)"},{"key":"D","text":"(4,−3)"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Adding the equations gives 3x = 12, so x = 4. Then y = x − 1 = 3. Both original equations are satisfied.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["28077444-a86b-578f-a01d-d683174a6783"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P006-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Systems of equations","lesson_subtopic":"Systems of equations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"ab951b70-9b72-5033-96e0-1e20086513ab","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"The graph of $y=\\frac{x^2-4}{x-2}$ has a removable discontinuity. At which point is the hole?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(−2,0)"},{"key":"B","text":"(2,0)"},{"key":"C","text":"(−2,4)"},{"key":"D","text":"(2,4)"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"For x ≠ 2, factor and cancel to obtain y = x + 2. The excluded input x = 2 would give y = 4, so the hole is (2,4).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["296355c1-7527-5138-9fc7-817c0fd90602"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P013-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Rational expressions","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"0fdeaf39-0f6c-5ee6-91a1-83d013db2bc1","track_id":"act2","topic":"Exponents, radicals and growth","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which expression equals $\\sqrt{72}$ in simplest radical form?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$3\\sqrt2$"},{"key":"B","text":"36"},{"key":"C","text":"$6\\sqrt2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$8\\sqrt3$"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"Since 72 = 36 × 2, √72 = √36 × √2 = 6√2. The radicand 2 has no perfect-square factor greater than 1.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["29abef4e-6d2b-598b-b3d7-8547eb71669f"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P015-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Exponents, radicals and growth","lesson_subtopic":"Exponents and radicals","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"5f1f6d29-2084-57f1-8954-4c6a146e70de","track_id":"act2","topic":"Matrices","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the inverse of $\\begin{pmatrix}3&1\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}-1&1\\\\2&-3\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}1&-1\\\\-2&3\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\\\2&3\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}3&-1\\\\-2&1\\end{pmatrix}$"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"The determinant is 3(1) − 1(2) = 1. The inverse is 1/determinant times the matrix obtained by swapping diagonal entries and negating off-diagonal entries, giving A.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["2c17ac10-8a80-5b26-a542-0a3a88b7a70f"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P026-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Matrices","lesson_subtopic":"Matrices","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"5f83503f-cebf-58fe-b24e-cc97379643a5","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the vertex of y = 2(x − 4)² − 7?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(4,−7)"},{"key":"B","text":"(−4,−7)"},{"key":"C","text":"(4,7)"},{"key":"D","text":"(2,−7)"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"In y = a(x − h)² + k, the vertex is (h,k). Here h = 4 and k = −7.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["317d7cf1-2ca9-50fb-bfdf-74d0d07fc006"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P004-Q019"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"bb29bf23-3231-5dba-be89-5e44d78d5df2","track_id":"act2","topic":"Inequalities and absolute value","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the complete solution set of |2x − 7| = 9?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"{1,8}"},{"key":"B","text":"{−8,1}"},{"key":"C","text":"{−1,1}"},{"key":"D","text":"{−1,8}"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Set 2x − 7 = 9 or 2x − 7 = −9. These give x = 8 or x = −1.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["36341e49-d169-59ba-8f93-ca0c9a8867ee"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P005-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Inequalities and absolute value","lesson_subtopic":"Inequalities and absolute value","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"ea79f566-d085-501f-a4ea-69347d318040","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A car travels 180 km at v km/h, then travels the same distance back at (v + 20) km/h, where v > 0. Which expression gives its total travel time in hours?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{180}{v}+\\frac{180}{20}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$180v+180(v+20)$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{180}{v}+\\frac{180}{v+20}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{360}{2v+20}$"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"For each leg, time = distance/speed. Add the outbound time 180/v and return time 180/(v + 20).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["38daac79-8b25-5a6e-924d-71c29e92e8f5"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P029-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Rational expressions","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"2bc02fd5-52c0-5b3d-8cab-423bc9707d26","track_id":"act2","topic":"Systems of equations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which ordered pair (x,y) solves 3x + 4 = −4y and x + 2y = 2?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(2,0)"},{"key":"B","text":"(−8,5)"},{"key":"C","text":"(8,−3)"},{"key":"D","text":"(−4,3)"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"From x + 2y = 2, x = 2 − 2y. Substitute into 3x + 4 = −4y: 10 − 6y = −4y, so y = 5 and x = −8.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["3ba6f5a2-9de0-5bd8-a70d-e37763fd5bad"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P032-Q081"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The solution is an ordered pair and the source supplies no choices; scalar numeric grading cannot grade the pair.","curriculum_lesson":"Systems of equations","lesson_subtopic":"Systems of equations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"ccb9dcb4-8320-5d0b-958c-56167c864119","track_id":"act2","topic":"Systems of equations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"The lines ax + 3y = 6 and 3x + 7y = −b intersect at (7,−4). What are a and b?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"a = 18/7, b = 7"},{"key":"B","text":"a = −18/7, b = 7"},{"key":"C","text":"a = 18/7, b = −7"},{"key":"D","text":"a = 6/7, b = 49"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Substitute the intersection: 7a − 12 = 6 gives a = 18/7. Also 21 − 28 = −b gives b = 7.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["3ec0a5f0-2e42-53d5-9bf6-2e27b9b2985d"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P040-Q105"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The prompt requests two parameter values and provides no choices; scalar numeric grading cannot grade both.","curriculum_lesson":"Systems of equations","lesson_subtopic":"Systems of equations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"48079742-6efe-5cd9-8dfb-d665c03075ad","track_id":"act2","topic":"Volume and surface area","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A cylinder has radius 4 units and height 9 units. What is its exact volume?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$36\\pi$"},{"key":"B","text":"$72\\pi$"},{"key":"C","text":"$324\\pi$"},{"key":"D","text":"$144\\pi$"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Cylinder volume is πr²h = π(4²)(9) = 144π cubic units.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["3f396c88-1a15-5528-a80d-4b6908ef651d"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P020-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Volume and surface area","lesson_subtopic":"Volume and surface area","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"86089731-aab4-5e69-9545-b3d151dfa5ba","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which is the complete factorization of 25x² − 121?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(5x − 11)²"},{"key":"B","text":"(5x + 11)²"},{"key":"C","text":"(5x − 11)(5x + 11)"},{"key":"D","text":"(25x − 11)(x + 11)"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"This is the difference of squares (5x)² − 11², which factors as (5x − 11)(5x + 11).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["451f180f-a518-5d02-bca5-5abe6f0be0a6"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P018-Q045"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Factored symbolic response has no choices and cannot be graded as a scalar numeric answer.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"d0deeb38-74cc-5679-b855-7e059204ccf2","track_id":"act2","topic":"Linear functions and slope","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the midpoint of the segment with endpoints (−3,7) and (5,−1)?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(−1,−3)"},{"key":"B","text":"(1,3)"},{"key":"C","text":"(4,−4)"},{"key":"D","text":"(2,6)"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Average the x-coordinates and y-coordinates separately: ((−3 + 5)/2, (7 − 1)/2) = (1,3).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["46097bfa-1393-513b-bb2a-502cd7452b48"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P019-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Linear functions and slope","lesson_subtopic":"Coordinate geometry","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"2e3e43ae-4974-5496-885d-9e08e426857d","track_id":"act2","topic":"Exponents, radicals and growth","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For x > 0, which expression equals $\\sqrt[3]{x^5}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$x^{5/3}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$x^{3/5}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$x^{15}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$x^2$"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"A cube root is a power of 1/3. Thus (x⁵)^(1/3) = x^(5/3). The explicit positive domain avoids differing conventions for fractional powers.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["4820eb3d-0cd3-5071-a436-6d0bfdd740c3"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P015-Q002"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Exponents, radicals and growth","lesson_subtopic":"Exponents and radicals","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"980d2e39-b4bc-5f94-98fb-cdf130df75fa","track_id":"act2","topic":"Linear functions and slope","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which equation has slope −2 and y-intercept 7?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"y = 2x + 7"},{"key":"B","text":"y = −2x − 7"},{"key":"C","text":"y = 7x − 2"},{"key":"D","text":"y = −2x + 7"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"In y = mx + b, the slope is m and y-intercept is b. Substitute m = −2 and b = 7.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["48c8b9b8-0a69-5c22-807c-42fb0ee01676"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P039-Q101"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: An equation is requested without choices; scalar numeric grading cannot grade it.","curriculum_lesson":"Linear functions and slope","lesson_subtopic":"Linear functions and slope","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"7503fb1e-bc67-5d05-9529-ee0fa3eaa80b","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the complete real solution set of $\\frac1x+\\frac1{x+2}=\\frac34$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\{\\frac43,2\\}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\{-4,2\\}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\{-\\frac43,2\\}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\{-2,0\\}$"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"The domain excludes x = 0 and x = −2. Multiplying by 4x(x + 2) gives 3x² − 2x − 8 = 0, or (3x + 4)(x − 2) = 0. Both −4/3 and 2 are allowed.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["49104dc3-4932-5524-93e7-84085561b37e"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P013-Q002"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Rational expressions","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"b6ef1b04-da89-501e-8457-c4aa712d7762","track_id":"act2","topic":"Complex numbers","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What are the solutions of x² + 4x + 13 = 0?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"−4 ± 13i"},{"key":"B","text":"−2 ± 3i"},{"key":"C","text":"2 ± 3i"},{"key":"D","text":"−2 ± 3"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Completing the square gives (x + 2)² = −9. Therefore x + 2 = ±3i and x = −2 ± 3i.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["59256413-ae79-52e9-9dd6-20dc9f415907"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P004-Q005"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Complex numbers","lesson_subtopic":"Complex numbers","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"7349c3ca-0363-5262-9898-0a00dc724b4c","track_id":"act2","topic":"Systems of equations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which ordered pair (x,y) solves x + y = 9 and 2x − y = 6?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(5,4)"},{"key":"B","text":"(4,5)"},{"key":"C","text":"(3,6)"},{"key":"D","text":"(6,3)"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Adding gives 3x = 15, so x = 5. Then y = 9 − 5 = 4.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["59721de1-67ec-5876-a650-5b4aa2b300d6"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P004-Q020"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Systems of equations","lesson_subtopic":"Systems of equations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"4210a4cc-e2ab-5a99-8beb-c0ff1a1e82d8","track_id":"act2","topic":"Complex numbers","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which expression equals $\\frac{3+2i}{1-i}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac52+\\frac12i$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac12-\\frac52i$"},{"key":"C","text":"$3+2i$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac12+\\frac52i$"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Multiply numerator and denominator by 1 + i. The denominator is 2; the numerator is 3 + 5i + 2i² = 1 + 5i. Divide by 2.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["5f033576-cad3-5794-a034-bfb20c353a99"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P012-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Complex numbers","lesson_subtopic":"Complex numbers","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"9949d0d3-4ef5-5efb-9909-cbb738769588","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which sequence of transformations takes y = f(x) to y = −2f(x + 3) + 5?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Shift left 3; compress vertically by 1/2; shift up 5"},{"key":"B","text":"Shift left 3; stretch vertically by 2 and reflect across the y-axis; shift down 5"},{"key":"C","text":"Shift left 3; stretch vertically by 2 and reflect across the x-axis; shift up 5"},{"key":"D","text":"Shift right 3; stretch vertically by 2 and reflect across the x-axis; shift up 5"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"The x + 3 shifts left 3. Multiplication by −2 stretches vertical distances by 2 and reflects across the x-axis. The final +5 shifts the result up 5.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["5f17833f-59b6-5a32-aae1-633a7b94b22b"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P019-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Functions and transformations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"17748abd-1dc8-519c-966d-8b19268844ac","track_id":"act2","topic":"Conic sections","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which conic is represented by 4x² − 9y² = 36?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Circle"},{"key":"B","text":"Hyperbola"},{"key":"C","text":"Ellipse"},{"key":"D","text":"Parabola"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Dividing by 36 gives x²/9 − y²/4 = 1. The squared terms have opposite signs, so the conic is a hyperbola.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["6037be14-ef15-5157-97d8-02acb6ed343a"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P024-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Conic sections","lesson_subtopic":"Conic sections","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"d6e5c1c8-c3a0-5539-9739-399e2ebb49b0","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the complete solution set of 2x² − 7x + 3 = 0?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"{1/2,3}"},{"key":"B","text":"{−1/2,−3}"},{"key":"C","text":"{1,3/2}"},{"key":"D","text":"{−1/2,3}"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Factor as (2x − 1)(x − 3) = 0. Thus x = 1/2 or x = 3.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["61a51dd3-cf3c-5b42-98bb-01fd84509e3e"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P010-Q002"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"46ed12b1-efe3-5097-83ec-87b624ddcb8f","track_id":"act2","topic":"Circles","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What are the center and radius of x² + y² − 6x + 8y − 11 = 0?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Center (−3,4), radius 6"},{"key":"B","text":"Center (3,−4), radius 36"},{"key":"C","text":"Center (3,4), radius 6"},{"key":"D","text":"Center (3,−4), radius 6"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Complete the squares: (x − 3)² + (y + 4)² = 11 + 9 + 16 = 36. The center is (3,−4) and radius √36 = 6.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["61c9e3fb-22bc-5c8d-9901-d94ffcee5ea2"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P024-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Circles","lesson_subtopic":"Circles","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"1d81f8b6-17db-5155-ad3d-a793d5a30bc6","track_id":"act2","topic":"Linear functions and slope","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Point (2,3) is reflected across the y-axis, then across the x-axis. What is the resulting point?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(2,−3)"},{"key":"B","text":"(3,2)"},{"key":"C","text":"(−2,−3)"},{"key":"D","text":"(−2,3)"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"The first reflection changes x to −2, producing (−2,3). The second changes y to −3, producing (−2,−3).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["69b73d1b-f316-59f3-8eaf-799f8e00226f"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P035-Q091"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The requested ordered-pair free response is not supported by scalar numeric grading.","curriculum_lesson":"Linear functions and slope","lesson_subtopic":"Coordinate geometry","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"ab16a410-6392-5656-a605-7d8c626a764c","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the inverse of f(x) = (x + 5)/3?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"f⁻¹(x) = (3 − x)/5"},{"key":"B","text":"f⁻¹(x) = 3x − 5"},{"key":"C","text":"f⁻¹(x) = 3x + 5"},{"key":"D","text":"f⁻¹(x) = (x − 5)/3"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Let y = (x + 5)/3. Then 3y = x + 5, so x = 3y − 5. Interchange x and y to obtain the inverse.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["6b29ba68-ed8f-5d95-8f94-3a747dc9884b"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P008-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Functions and transformations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"b7c5a438-c1d9-5423-8514-dd3226282ced","track_id":"act2","topic":"Triangles and similarity","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A 30°–60°–90° triangle has short leg 7. What are its hypotenuse and long leg, respectively?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$14,\\ 7\\sqrt3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$7\\sqrt3,\\ 14$"},{"key":"C","text":"$14,\\ 7\\sqrt2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$7,\\ 14$"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"The side ratio short : long : hypotenuse is 1 : √3 : 2. Multiplying by 7 gives hypotenuse 14 and long leg 7√3.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["6c698a69-c0ab-5b1a-b503-43b48529cfb2"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P021-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles and similarity","lesson_subtopic":"Triangles and similarity","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"5fa6193a-29ad-5157-8a3b-7a573b2e55a8","track_id":"act2","topic":"Ratios, percentages and unit conversion","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Sarah invests $5,000 at a simple annual interest rate of 3%. Which expression gives the interest earned, in dollars, after t years?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5000 + 150t"},{"key":"B","text":"5000(1.03)ᵗ"},{"key":"C","text":"150(1.03)ᵗ"},{"key":"D","text":"150t"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Simple interest is principal × annual rate × time: 5000 × 0.03 × t = 150t. The question asks for interest, not the total account balance.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["737364bf-2739-5a73-b908-50a94bc81ddd"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D17-P031-Q031"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Source has no answer choices. The interest is 150t, but no source-faithful MCQ can be released.","curriculum_lesson":"Ratios, percentages and unit conversion","lesson_subtopic":"Ratios, percentages and unit conversion","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"d7a16540-0ed6-58fa-a0d8-09a0f4528162","track_id":"act2","topic":"Area and perimeter","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A rectangle has perimeter 80 units and width w units, where 0 < w < 40. Which expression gives its area?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"40w"},{"key":"B","text":"2w(40 − w)"},{"key":"C","text":"w(40 − w)"},{"key":"D","text":"w(80 − w)"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"From 2(length + width) = 80, length = 40 − w. Area is length × width = w(40 − w).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["7e911655-761e-5421-adf0-fcb38a8d2152"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P029-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Area and perimeter","lesson_subtopic":"Area and perimeter","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"45f52837-6f8e-5f66-80c1-189c51b93400","track_id":"act2","topic":"Trigonometry","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For y = −3 cos(4x) + 2, with x measured in radians, what are the amplitude and period?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$2,\\ \\pi/2$"},{"key":"B","text":"$3,\\ \\pi/2$"},{"key":"C","text":"$-3,\\ \\pi/2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$3,\\ 8\\pi$"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"The amplitude is the absolute value of −3, which is 3. Period is 2π/|4| = π/2. The vertical shift does not change either quantity.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["7f518a2a-d7b8-5640-9702-bbcaaa987992"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P022-Q002"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Trigonometry","lesson_subtopic":"Trigonometry","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"78cb4eb4-82a3-5a95-9e72-f90cc865f3f6","track_id":"act2","topic":"Exponents, radicals and growth","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For nonzero x and y, which expression equals $\\frac{6x^3y^{-2}}{3x^{-1}y}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{2x^4}{y^3}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{2x^2}{y}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2x^4y^3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{3x^4}{y^3}$"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Divide coefficients to get 2. Subtract exponents when dividing: x^(3 − (−1)) = x⁴ and y^(−2 − 1) = y⁻³. Therefore the result is 2x⁴/y³.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["84d52170-2e92-51ec-a620-42197786d56a"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P005-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Exponents, radicals and growth","lesson_subtopic":"Exponents and radicals","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"7bd37aec-acba-5916-a75c-92c5a9c04090","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For x ≠ 3 and x ≠ −2, which expression equals $\\frac{x^2-9}{x^2-x-6}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{x-3}{x+2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{x+3}{x-2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$x+3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{x+3}{x+2}$"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Factor the numerator as (x − 3)(x + 3) and denominator as (x − 3)(x + 2). Cancel the common factor while retaining both original domain exclusions.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["89153e97-2b10-59c9-8e19-494a3f97c1b8"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P013-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Rational expressions","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"cee68d87-128b-50eb-a847-596666a592a2","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which is the complete factorization of x³ − 4x² − x + 4?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(x − 4)(x − 1)²"},{"key":"B","text":"(x − 4)(x² + 1)"},{"key":"C","text":"(x − 4)(x − 1)(x + 1)"},{"key":"D","text":"(x + 4)(x − 1)(x + 1)"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"Group terms: x²(x − 4) − (x − 4) = (x − 4)(x² − 1). Factor the difference of squares.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["8b343527-1eac-5295-925b-1dfc4d2730a3"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P012-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"d9b9f20b-cf36-54c6-8cfc-924c6a2a2980","track_id":"act2","topic":"Angles and polygons","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A simple polygon has an interior-angle sum of 540°. How many sides does it have?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"8"},{"key":"B","text":"5"},{"key":"C","text":"4"},{"key":"D","text":"6"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"For n sides, the sum is (n − 2)180°. Solving (n − 2)180 = 540 gives n = 5.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["8b8cfb7a-6df2-5ee6-a045-80a1ef7a79af"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P030-Q077"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The prompt asks for a polygon name, has no choices, and cannot be graded as a scalar numeric response.","curriculum_lesson":"Angles and polygons","lesson_subtopic":"Angles and polygons","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"91fa78d1-f523-54d9-b3b4-1bcb41333de0","track_id":"act2","topic":"Linear functions and slope","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the reflection of (6,−2) across the line y = x?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(−2,6)"},{"key":"B","text":"(2,−6)"},{"key":"C","text":"(−6,2)"},{"key":"D","text":"(6,2)"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Reflection across y = x interchanges the coordinates: (x,y) becomes (y,x).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["90f77567-6ac9-5fcb-829b-82cfb02c298a"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P019-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Linear functions and slope","lesson_subtopic":"Coordinate geometry","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"db18c258-0bbc-5d41-9b59-190f17b111dd","track_id":"act2","topic":"Conic sections","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What are the vertices on the major axis of $\\frac{x^2}{25}+\\frac{y^2}{9}=1$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(0,−5) and (0,5)"},{"key":"B","text":"(−3,0) and (3,0)"},{"key":"C","text":"(−4,0) and (4,0)"},{"key":"D","text":"(−5,0) and (5,0)"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"The larger denominator is 25 beneath x², so the major axis is horizontal and semimajor length is √25 = 5. The center is (0,0), giving vertices (±5,0).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["967c3d8b-4109-5b7a-9c45-1b287d076018"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P024-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Conic sections","lesson_subtopic":"Conic sections","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"18119073-f571-5c55-a2cf-6a83db3a86be","track_id":"act2","topic":"Inequalities and absolute value","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the solution set of −3 ≤ 2x + 5 < 11?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"−8 ≤ x < 6"},{"key":"B","text":"−1 ≤ x < 8"},{"key":"C","text":"−4 ≤ x < 3"},{"key":"D","text":"−4 < x ≤ 3"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"Subtract 5 throughout: −8 ≤ 2x < 6. Divide throughout by positive 2, retaining the inequality directions and endpoint types.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["9a06ec43-8291-520f-b1e8-0b6657539920"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P006-Q002"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Inequalities and absolute value","lesson_subtopic":"Inequalities and absolute value","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"dde33c79-fe47-5df6-ba8f-a68a50dee896","track_id":"act2","topic":"Trigonometry","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"In a right triangle, the side opposite acute angle θ is 9 and the hypotenuse is 15. What are sin θ and cos θ, respectively?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5/3 and 5/4"},{"key":"B","text":"3/5 and 4/5"},{"key":"C","text":"4/5 and 3/5"},{"key":"D","text":"3/5 and 5/4"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"The adjacent side is √(15² − 9²) = 12. Thus sin θ = 9/15 = 3/5 and cos θ = 12/15 = 4/5.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["9dff9f8a-d5d3-548f-9436-909b22aa29a2"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P021-Q002"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Trigonometry","lesson_subtopic":"Trigonometry","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"bdc3e17f-8827-5d66-8b3f-40edf958caa8","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which is the vertex form of y = x² − 6x + 5?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"y = (x − 3)² − 4"},{"key":"B","text":"y = (x + 3)² − 4"},{"key":"C","text":"y = (x − 3)² + 5"},{"key":"D","text":"y = (x − 6)² − 31"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Complete the square: x² − 6x + 5 = (x² − 6x + 9) − 4 = (x − 3)² − 4.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["9fcd9239-7ac9-5e0c-9251-e69e7f973de5"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P010-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"451af467-5eb5-5ab8-8355-b233d3e62ef6","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which is the complete factorization of x² − 7x + 12?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(x + 3)(x + 4)"},{"key":"B","text":"(x − 2)(x − 6)"},{"key":"C","text":"(x + 3)(x − 4)"},{"key":"D","text":"(x − 3)(x − 4)"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"The numbers −3 and −4 multiply to 12 and add to −7, so the factorization is (x − 3)(x − 4).","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["a77b0768-4443-5d3d-aa74-b8f53201f661"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P004-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"217fb843-bd9e-5959-804c-f60285e94a55","track_id":"act2","topic":"Trigonometry","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What are all solutions of sin x = 1/2 in the interval 0 ≤ x < 2π, with x in radians?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\pi/3,\\ 2\\pi/3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$5\\pi/6,\\ 11\\pi/6$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\pi/6,\\ 5\\pi/6$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\pi/6,\\ 7\\pi/6$"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"The reference angle is π/6. Sine is positive in Quadrants I and II, so the solutions are π/6 and π − π/6 = 5π/6.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["a9517d0e-8c62-5ce3-853c-065976dca334"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P022-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Trigonometry","lesson_subtopic":"Trigonometry","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"f3e9bdd2-f4be-5d2e-95af-d3aeff829ec3","track_id":"act2","topic":"Logic and sets","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which statement is the converse of “If Chris uses toothpaste X, then Chris does not get cavities”?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"If Chris uses toothpaste X, then Chris gets cavities"},{"key":"B","text":"If Chris does not get cavities, then Chris uses toothpaste X"},{"key":"C","text":"If Chris does not use toothpaste X, then Chris gets cavities"},{"key":"D","text":"If Chris gets cavities, then Chris does not use toothpaste X"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"The converse of “if P, then Q” is “if Q, then P.” Interchange the hypothesis and conclusion without negating either. This asks about logical form, not the truth of the converse.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["abe5dbb4-442a-5d6e-950b-c57b4f43944f"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P011-Q026"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Textual converse free response has no choices and is not supported by numeric grading.","curriculum_lesson":"Logic and sets","lesson_subtopic":"Logic","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"4c2ecf7a-dc1e-5c10-af6f-70d4b00a60d7","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A 4 m by 6 m rectangular garden is surrounded on all sides by a sidewalk of uniform width w. The combined garden-and-sidewalk area is 40 m². What is the exact positive width w?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{41}-5}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{41}+5}{2}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\sqrt{41}-5$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{41}-10}{2}$"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"The outer dimensions are 4 + 2w and 6 + 2w. Their product equals 40, so w² + 5w − 4 = 0. The quadratic formula gives (−5 ± √41)/2. Only (√41 − 5)/2 is positive.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["abf3a097-3ae1-56da-99ef-12337dd810a9"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D17-P030-Q030"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Source has no answer choices; sidewalk width solves (4+2w)(6+2w)=40, giving (√41−5)/2. Cannot create options.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"09c043f9-ccbc-58c6-9312-4d208ca0aa10","track_id":"act2","topic":"Circles","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which equation describes a circle centered at (2,−3) with radius 5?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(x + 2)² + (y − 3)² = 25"},{"key":"B","text":"(x − 2)² + (y + 3)² = 5"},{"key":"C","text":"(x − 2)² + (y − 3)² = 25"},{"key":"D","text":"(x − 2)² + (y + 3)² = 25"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Use (x − h)² + (y − k)² = r² with h = 2, k = −3, and r = 5.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["cb5328b0-077c-5913-80b3-a38f57a9f966"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P004-Q014"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Circles","lesson_subtopic":"Circles","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"dba9d962-bfde-5bcc-a59c-98d61bf2cf8f","track_id":"act2","topic":"Linear functions and slope","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which equation represents the line through (2,5) with slope −3?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"y = 3x − 1"},{"key":"B","text":"y = −3x + 5"},{"key":"C","text":"y = −3x + 11"},{"key":"D","text":"y = −3x − 1"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"Point-slope form gives y − 5 = −3(x − 2). Expanding gives y = −3x + 11.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["d4fabad7-80c7-5751-8297-f0e25fe17be4"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P006-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Linear functions and slope","lesson_subtopic":"Linear functions and slope","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"e5d336a1-bdbc-5e32-ac54-120c903ea19d","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which quadratic polynomial has roots 2 and −5 and leading coefficient 3?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"3x² + 9x + 30"},{"key":"B","text":"3x² + 9x − 30"},{"key":"C","text":"3x² − 9x − 30"},{"key":"D","text":"x² + 3x − 10"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"The polynomial is 3(x − 2)(x + 5) = 3(x² + 3x − 10) = 3x² + 9x − 30.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["dc91cd5c-f2db-56e1-843d-40c3885626f4"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P030-Q001"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"8557177e-b947-5303-8ba1-38bb80c5df50","track_id":"act2","topic":"Logarithms and exponentials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A population initially has 500 members and increases by 6% each year. Which function gives its population after t years?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"P(t) = 500(1.06)ᵗ"},{"key":"B","text":"P(t) = 500(0.06)ᵗ"},{"key":"C","text":"P(t) = 500 + 6t"},{"key":"D","text":"P(t) = 500(0.94)ᵗ"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"A 6% annual increase multiplies the previous population by 1.06 each year. Starting at 500 gives P(t) = 500(1.06)ᵗ.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["dde56c95-4d24-50a6-9fd0-9e867f49e16c"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P004-Q018"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Logarithms and exponentials","lesson_subtopic":"Logarithms and exponentials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"49dafa85-8ab9-5cef-8a7d-707724ce5b6a","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What are the domain and range of y = |x| + 1?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Domain: x ≥ 0; range: y ≥ 1"},{"key":"B","text":"Domain: all real numbers; range: y > 1"},{"key":"C","text":"Domain: x ≥ 1; range: all real numbers"},{"key":"D","text":"Domain: all real numbers; range: y ≥ 1"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Absolute value is defined for every real x and is always nonnegative. Its minimum is 0 at x = 0, so y has minimum 1 and no upper bound.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["de4a2e58-5250-542d-8ca1-133cdfc3a22e"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P057-Q141"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The request asks for both a domain and range with no choices; scalar numeric grading is unsuitable.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Functions and transformations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"2ab9b29c-73e8-5cca-baf0-8704640ec733","track_id":"act2","topic":"Exponents, radicals and growth","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which expression equals $\\frac5{2+\\sqrt3}$ and has a rational denominator?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$5-2\\sqrt3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{10-5\\sqrt3}{7}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$10-5\\sqrt3$"},{"key":"D","text":"$10+5\\sqrt3$"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"Multiply numerator and denominator by 2 − √3. The denominator becomes 4 − 3 = 1, leaving 5(2 − √3) = 10 − 5√3.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["e6c907a4-339c-575b-a5ec-d9cb4bedea4f"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P015-Q003"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Exponents, radicals and growth","lesson_subtopic":"Exponents and radicals","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"1dfe0bc6-fdc2-5a93-be80-c539bcc4105b","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For x ≠ 3, which expression equals $\\frac{x^2-9}{x-3}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"x + 9"},{"key":"B","text":"x + 3"},{"key":"C","text":"x − 3"},{"key":"D","text":"x² + 3"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Factor x² − 9 = (x − 3)(x + 3). Since x ≠ 3, cancel x − 3 to obtain x + 3.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["e81728fa-0bfe-500a-b95c-b6a596921bac"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P004-Q006"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Rational expressions","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"60734574-7b82-5d2f-a926-bc0f2438319b","track_id":"act2","topic":"Inequalities and absolute value","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which inequality has the same solution set as x + 8 ≥ 7 + 2x?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"x ≤ 1"},{"key":"B","text":"x ≥ 1"},{"key":"C","text":"x ≤ −1"},{"key":"D","text":"x ≥ −1"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Subtract x + 7 from both sides to obtain 1 ≥ x, which is x ≤ 1. Equality at x = 1 is included.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["ec0b80b3-e678-57ca-b685-9f71dd1510b9"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P040-Q104"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The request is to draw a number line, which cannot be graded by scalar numeric entry.","curriculum_lesson":"Inequalities and absolute value","lesson_subtopic":"Inequalities and absolute value","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"03dfebba-f5bd-5db9-943b-a25b7ca37ffd","track_id":"act2","topic":"Statistics and data analysis","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What are the mean and median, respectively, of 3, 5, 5, 7, and 10?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"5 and 6"},{"key":"B","text":"6 and 6"},{"key":"C","text":"5 and 5"},{"key":"D","text":"6 and 5"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"The sum is 30, so the mean is 30/5 = 6. The third value in the sorted list is 5, so the median is 5.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["ed1dcc2d-a539-533b-82a8-53b453cd19f7"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P027-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics and data analysis","lesson_subtopic":"Statistics and data analysis","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"53629c27-7f2b-57dd-9eaf-eeb72d00ad8f","track_id":"act2","topic":"Matrices","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is $\\begin{pmatrix}1&2\\\\0&3\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}4&1\\\\-2&5\\end{pmatrix}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}0&9\\\\-6&15\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}4&11\\\\-6&15\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}0&11\\\\-6&15\\end{pmatrix}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\begin{pmatrix}4&2\\\\0&15\\end{pmatrix}$"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"Multiply rows by columns: top-left 1(4) + 2(−2) = 0; top-right 1(1) + 2(5) = 11; bottom-left 0(4) + 3(−2) = −6; bottom-right 0(1) + 3(5) = 15.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["f8d3bf78-537b-594e-bc5c-f4bef8bf23a6"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D56-P026-Q004"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Symbolic, multi-part or descriptive open response has no original MCQ choices; retain solution until supported input is provided.","curriculum_lesson":"Matrices","lesson_subtopic":"Matrices","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"a2f005b1-b3bd-5066-8916-9980e0cc6379","track_id":"act2","topic":"Inequalities and absolute value","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which inequality describes exactly the solution set of −3x + 7 < 16?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"x > −9"},{"key":"B","text":"x > −3"},{"key":"C","text":"x < −3"},{"key":"D","text":"x < −9"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Subtract 7: −3x < 9. Divide by −3 and reverse the inequality to get x > −3. Although x > −9 follows from the solution, it includes extra values and is not the exact solution set.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["31ddb28a-8c1d-5808-bccc-f47d68f96c41","ae11aecb-8844-5bdf-9dec-7f21b4c25fad"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D52-P013-Q061","ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D23-P005-Q075"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Both A (x>−3) and D (x>−9) must be true from −3x+7<16, so the printed MCQ has multiple correct choices.","curriculum_lesson":"Inequalities and absolute value","lesson_subtopic":"Inequalities and absolute value","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"fbeeabb3-36f0-5a7d-bccf-ea9a8a5ab859","track_id":"act2","topic":"Inequalities and absolute value","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A craft shop spends less than $360 on bracelet and necklace kits. Each bracelet kit costs $6 and each necklace kit costs $12. It buys at least 8 more bracelet kits than necklace kits. Which purchase satisfies both conditions?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"28 bracelet kits and 22 necklace kits"},{"key":"B","text":"30 bracelet kits and 18 necklace kits"},{"key":"C","text":"20 bracelet kits and 15 necklace kits"},{"key":"D","text":"30 bracelet kits and 10 necklace kits"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"For D, cost = 6(30) + 12(10) = 300, which is less than 360; the difference is 20, which is at least 8. A and B exceed the budget. C meets the budget but its difference is only 5. The options are explicitly corrected instructor choices.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["3eff8a14-c778-5c68-b2d6-c4eda2007af4"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D53-P005-Q011"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: No listed option satisfies both constraints.","curriculum_lesson":"Inequalities and absolute value","lesson_subtopic":"Inequalities and absolute value","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"06c760a1-e61a-5109-9296-801757302007","track_id":"act2","topic":"Inequalities and absolute value","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the complete real solution set of $\\left|\\frac{2-x}{7}\\right|=\\left|\\frac{x+3}{5}\\right|$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\{-\\frac{11}{12}\\}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\{\\frac{11}{12},\\frac{31}{2}\\}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\{-\\frac{11}{12},\\frac{11}{6}\\}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\{-\\frac{11}{12},-\\frac{31}{2}\\}$"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Equal absolute values mean the quantities are equal or opposite. From 5(2 − x) = 7(x + 3), x = −11/12. From 5(2 − x) = −7(x + 3), x = −31/2. Both must be included.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["6dc9e13a-f3bd-5f3a-a2cf-c9f11660f0cb","f452b8ea-1e95-5d3b-ada2-a4b7aa48a75e"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D23-P008-Q089","ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D52-P015-Q072"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The source equation has absolute values on both sides. Solving gives x=-11/12 or x=-31/2. No listed set contains both; optionB omits the second root and optionC has an incorrect second value.","curriculum_lesson":"Inequalities and absolute value","lesson_subtopic":"Inequalities and absolute value","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"ec1fe096-170f-557c-9ae4-2047f109c798","track_id":"act2","topic":"Functions and transformations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which function has x-intercept (−1,0) and horizontal asymptote y = −3?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$f(x)=\\frac{3(x+1)}{x+2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$f(x)=\\frac{-3(x+2)}{x+1}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$f(x)=\\frac{-3(x+1)}{x+2}$"},{"key":"D","text":"$f(x)=\\frac{-3(x-1)}{x+2}$"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"For A, x = −1 makes the numerator zero and leaves denominator 1, so the intercept is (−1,0). The ratio of leading coefficients is −3, giving horizontal asymptote y = −3. The other options fail at least one condition.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["7e080c5c-2b38-577d-bc87-d25a193c5a3e"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D06-P014-Q007"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: No option satisfies both conditions. B and C have horizontal asymptote -3/2 but do not vanish at x=-1; D vanishes at -1 but has horizontal asymptote -15/2.","curriculum_lesson":"Functions and transformations","lesson_subtopic":"Functions and transformations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"f3504d47-86ba-5207-97eb-37329e867c10","track_id":"act2","topic":"Statistics and data analysis","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Dan’s first five scores are 70, 80, 80, 70, and 75. The scores 90 and 95 are added to form one cumulative seven-score data set. Relative to the original five scores, how do its mean and median change?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Both increase by 10"},{"key":"B","text":"Both increase by 5"},{"key":"C","text":"The mean increases by 5 and the median stays the same"},{"key":"D","text":"The mean stays the same and the median increases by 5"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"The original sum is 375, mean 75, and median 75. The new sum is 560, mean 560/7 = 80, and median 80. Both increase by 5. The cumulative interpretation is explicitly stated.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["7f8050b5-15b3-5463-8676-bbb0257a27ee"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P025-Q060"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The source is ambiguous about whether the after-tutoring set consists of the two new scores or all seven scores. The literal two-score set gives no listed answer.","curriculum_lesson":"Statistics and data analysis","lesson_subtopic":"Statistics and data analysis","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"f38c0869-5d24-5c03-8fc1-9c450d34fb4f","track_id":"act2","topic":"Quadratics and polynomials","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the complete real solution set of 2x² − 15 = −6?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\{-\\frac{3\\sqrt2}{2},\\frac{3\\sqrt2}{2}\\}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\{-\\sqrt3,\\sqrt3\\}$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\{-\\sqrt6,\\sqrt6\\}$"},{"key":"D","text":"{−6,6}"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"Add 15 and divide by 2 to obtain x² = 9/2. Thus x = ±√(9/2) = ±3√2/2. These corrected choices include both roots.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["810b6716-8724-5d85-81c4-5006f1f97ef5"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P055-Q138"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: None of the listed answers solves the printed equation.","curriculum_lesson":"Quadratics and polynomials","lesson_subtopic":"Quadratics and polynomials","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"d84343dd-dcb4-57cc-bd36-0d8b0b9cade5","track_id":"act2","topic":"Exponents, radicals and growth","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For nonzero x and y, which expression equals $\\frac{x^{16}y^9+x^6y^2}{x^2y^2}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$x^{14}y^7+x^4y$"},{"key":"B","text":"$x^8y^7+x^3$"},{"key":"C","text":"$x^{18}y^{11}+x^8y^4$"},{"key":"D","text":"$x^{14}y^7+x^4$"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Divide each numerator term by x²y². Subtracting exponents gives x¹⁴y⁷ and x⁴, respectively. The second term has no remaining factor of y.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["8bcc0c58-4a45-5c07-8295-5f9e8197a447"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D21-P071-Q041"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: No listed answer is correct. B has an extra factor y in its second term; do not silently repair.","curriculum_lesson":"Exponents, radicals and growth","lesson_subtopic":"Exponents and radicals","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"ae5c13e3-84e1-58c7-9da5-5ec1d52e7525","track_id":"act2","topic":"Exponents, radicals and growth","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For x ≠ 0 and y > 0, which expression equals $\\frac{2x^2y}{x\\sqrt y}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt y}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$2xy$"},{"key":"C","text":"$2x\\sqrt y$"},{"key":"D","text":"$2x^2\\sqrt y$"}],"correct":"C","explanation":"Cancel one factor of x. Since y/√y = √y for y > 0, the expression becomes 2x√y. The choices are corrected so only one is equivalent on the stated domain.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["a085f287-90e7-5005-9f88-1f77549cb994"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-OFFICIAL-20261029-M1-P2-Q19"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Blocked: on the original real domain x!=0,y>0, 2x^2*y/(x*sqrt(y))=2xy/sqrt(y)=2x*sqrt(y). Both A and B are equivalent, so this is not a valid single-answer item.","curriculum_lesson":"Exponents, radicals and growth","lesson_subtopic":"Exponents and radicals","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"9a0343f1-04dd-56e4-b6fc-a885ca0ae4f0","track_id":"act2","topic":"Exponents, radicals and growth","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"Which expression equals $\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{\\sqrt2}$?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"$\\frac{15}{2}$"},{"key":"B","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}2$"},{"key":"C","text":"$\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}2$"},{"key":"D","text":"$\\sqrt{30}$"}],"correct":"B","explanation":"Multiply numerator and denominator by √2 to get √30/2. The source’s second equivalent option has been replaced with an explicit instructor-authored distractor.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["aacba8d8-0f1e-5a41-b7bc-f4b401e9bd24"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D21-P017-Q052"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The source asks only to simplify, but options B, $\\sqrt{30}/2$, and C, $\\sqrt{7.5}$, are both exactly equal to $\\sqrt{15}/\\sqrt2$. There is no unique correct choice. The question is repeated at D21-P047-Q018.","curriculum_lesson":"Exponents, radicals and growth","lesson_subtopic":"Exponents and radicals","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"cefc1468-7880-55a1-9eb2-d84b876b5c60","track_id":"act2","topic":"Systems of equations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"A cabinet contains 15 plates. Each has diameter 7 inches or 12 inches, and the sum of the 15 diameters is 140 inches. Let x count the 7-inch plates and y count the 12-inch plates. Which system models this situation?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"x + y = 15; 7x + 12y = 140"},{"key":"B","text":"x + y = 140; 7x + 12y = 15"},{"key":"C","text":"x + y = 15; 12x + 7y = 140"},{"key":"D","text":"7x + y = 15; x + 12y = 140"}],"correct":"A","explanation":"The plate count gives x + y = 15. Summing diameters gives 7x + 12y = 140. These equations have the valid integer solution x = 8, y = 7. This instructor adaptation explicitly corrects the impossible printed total of 14 inches to 140 inches.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["af2c2124-569a-56d4-9b36-a22cf8f089cd"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D14-P006-Q015"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: Printed stem says the total diameters of 15 plates of diameter 7 or 12 inches is 14 inches; this is impossible. Options use 140, which would require correcting the source.","curriculum_lesson":"Systems of equations","lesson_subtopic":"Systems of equations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}},{"id":"ad96f85f-6241-54dd-8d5b-0d1d297676a9","track_id":"act2","topic":"Systems of equations","difficulty":"medium","type":"mcq","stem":"For a nonzero real constant a, which ordered pair (x,y) solves x + ay = 2 and 3x − 2ay = 6?","choices":[{"key":"A","text":"(0,2/a)"},{"key":"B","text":"(−2,0)"},{"key":"C","text":"(2,2/a)"},{"key":"D","text":"(2,0)"}],"correct":"D","explanation":"Multiply the first equation by 3 and subtract the second: 5ay = 0. Since a ≠ 0, y = 0, and then x = 2. The nonzero condition is explicitly added to exclude the infinitely-many-solutions case a = 0.","assets":{"source":"Ghoneem Math — supported-response instructor adaptation","source_ids_adapted":["ec6acdfa-1dab-561f-ab3a-fd7a542c2ea6"],"source_codes_adapted":["ACT2-IMPORT-20261030-D20-P041-Q108"],"content_origin":"instructor_adaptation","adaptation_reason":"Explicit instructor-authored multiple-choice repair. Fully specified mathematics is retained or the added condition/corrected datum is stated explicitly in the explanation. No missing diagram is inferred. Original source remains held. Source blocker: The parameter a is unrestricted, so when a=0 the system has infinitely many solutions; two choices also contain an unbound y/a. A unique complete solution cannot be certified without adding assumptions.","curriculum_lesson":"Systems of equations","lesson_subtopic":"Systems of equations","verified_release":"20261114-bank-supported-responses","answer_review_status":"independently_solved","figure_required":false,"bank_review_date":"2026-11-14"}}]}'::jsonb;
 p jsonb; before_q jsonb; before_k jsonb; h text; t text; old_history jsonb := '{}';
 protected_tables text[] := array['attempts','attempt_answers','attempt_results','exams','assignments','revision_sessions','practice_bundle_items','practice_notebook'];
 updated_count int := 0; added_count int := 0;
begin
 -- Lock only the affected question/key rows, in a stable order, before checking hashes.
 perform 1 from questions where id in (select (v->>'id')::uuid from jsonb_array_elements(data_->'updates') v) order by id for update;
 perform 1 from question_keys where question_id in (select (v->>'id')::uuid from jsonb_array_elements(data_->'updates') v) order by question_id for update;
 for p in select value from jsonb_array_elements(data_->'updates') loop
   select to_jsonb(x) into before_q from questions x where id=(p->>'id')::uuid;
   select to_jsonb(x) into before_k from question_keys x where question_id=(p->>'id')::uuid;
   if before_q is null or before_k is null or md5(before_q::text) is distinct from p->>'row_hash' or md5(before_k::text) is distinct from p->>'key_hash'
   then raise exception 'Concurrent content change: %',p->>'id'; end if;
 end loop;
 for p in select value from jsonb_array_elements(data_->'additions') loop
   if exists(select 1 from questions where id=(p->>'id')::uuid) then raise exception 'Adaptation already exists: %',p->>'id'; end if;
   if exists(select 1 from questions x where x.assets->'source_ids_adapted' ?| array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(p->'assets'->'source_ids_adapted')))
   then raise exception 'Source already has an adaptation: %',p->>'id'; end if;
 end loop;
 -- The three clarified statements had no submitted answers at review time.
 if exists(select 1 from attempt_answers where question_id=any(array['38b3ea7c-1a64-5d12-8944-dedd2448b7c9','2574795c-0842-5799-a7a6-9f318be55de6','df2132af-840a-501e-9268-3a64a7d75791']::uuid[]))
 then raise exception 'New answers require separate versioning before clarification'; end if;
 if exists(select 1 from attempts a join exams e on e.id=a.exam_id where a.status='in_progress' and e.question_ids && array['38b3ea7c-1a64-5d12-8944-dedd2448b7c9','2574795c-0842-5799-a7a6-9f318be55de6','df2132af-840a-501e-9268-3a64a7d75791']::uuid[])
 then raise exception 'Active exam requires separate versioning before clarification'; end if;
 foreach t in array protected_tables loop
   execute format('select md5(coalesce(string_agg(h, %L order by h),%L)) from (select md5(to_jsonb(x)::text) h from public.%I x) s','','',t) into h;
   old_history := old_history || jsonb_build_object(t,h);
 end loop;
 for p in select value from jsonb_array_elements(data_->'updates') loop
   update questions set
    stem=case when p->'fields' ? 'stem' then p->'fields'->>'stem' else stem end,
    choices=case when p->'fields' ? 'choices' then p->'fields'->'choices' else choices end,
    assets=(assets - array(select jsonb_array_elements_text(p->'assets_remove'))) || (p->'assets_merge')
   where id=(p->>'id')::uuid;
   if p->'fields' ? 'explanation' then
    update question_keys set explanation=p->'fields'->>'explanation' where question_id=(p->>'id')::uuid;
   end if;
   updated_count:=updated_count+1;
 end loop;
 for p in select value from jsonb_array_elements(data_->'additions') loop
   insert into questions(id,track_id,topic,difficulty,type,stem,choices,assets)
    values((p->>'id')::uuid,p->>'track_id',p->>'topic',p->>'difficulty',p->>'type',p->>'stem',p->'choices',p->'assets');
   insert into question_keys(question_id,correct,explanation) values((p->>'id')::uuid,p->'correct',p->>'explanation');
   added_count:=added_count+1;
 end loop;
 if updated_count<>73 or added_count<>70 then raise exception 'Unexpected release size'; end if;
 if exists(select 1 from questions q left join question_keys k on k.question_id=q.id
   where q.assets->>'verified_release'=data_->>'release' and not portal_private.question_eligible(q,k,q.track_id,false))
 then raise exception 'Release contains ineligible content'; end if;
 if (select count(*) from questions where assets->>'verified_release'=data_->>'release')<>70 then raise exception 'Unexpected verified release count'; end if;
 foreach t in array protected_tables loop
   execute format('select md5(coalesce(string_agg(h, %L order by h),%L)) from (select md5(to_jsonb(x)::text) h from public.%I x) s','','',t) into h;
   if h is distinct from old_history->>t then raise exception 'Protected assessment history changed: %',t; end if;
 end loop;
end $release$;
commit;
